      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Senator Halloway stood calmly over the holographic projections, his voice a low, steady rhythm that outlined the logic of national security with surgical precision. \"The metrics are clear, Kai: without this predictive AI, the surveillance time required to stop a bioterrorism event exceeds the pathogen's incubation period by weeks; we simply cannot allow humanity to operate on the slow pace of democracy when survival is on the line.\"\n\"It's not about survival, it's about *who* decides what a crime is!\" Kai shoved a tablet into the air, her voice rising in a disjointed cascade of fears she hadn't organized into a real argument. \"If we don't know my father's location, then our money is stolen, so that's bad, but then who owns the people? Well, the corporation does, which is why—um—why I need this! Is it the government? Is that why I am not supposed to be here?\"\nSenator Halloway didn't flinch at her chaos, instead tapping a finger to highlight a single, unblinking stat that dismissed her entire worldview. \"Any system with perfect intelligence is a system of absolute order; we do not trade privacy for power because we are not",
